            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 1. Classical Bit vs Qubit\n",
                "\n",
                "A classical bit can be either `0` or `1`.\n",
                "\n",
                "A qubit can be in a quantum state that is a combination of `0` and `1` until it is measured.\n",
                "\n",
                "When measured, the qubit collapses to a classical value: either `0` or `1`.\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "from qiskit import QuantumCircuit\n",
                "from qiskit_aer import AerSimulator\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Qiskit imported successfully\")\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2. A Single Qubit Circuit\n",
                "\n",
                "We start with one qubit and one classical bit.\n",
                "\n",
                "By default, the qubit starts in state `|0>`.\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "qc = QuantumCircuit(1, 1)\n",
                "qc.measure(0, 0)\n",
                "\n",
                "qc.draw(\"mpl\")\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "simulator = AerSimulator()\n",
                "result = simulator.run(qc, shots=1024).result()\n",
                "counts = result.get_counts()\n",
                "\n",
                "counts\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Expected result: almost all measurements should return `0`, because the qubit was initialized in `|0>` and no gate was applied before measurement.\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3. The X Gate\n",
                "\n",
                "The X gate is similar to a classical NOT gate.\n",
                "\n",
                "It transforms:\n",
                "\n",
                "- `|0>` into `|1>`\n",
                "- `|1>` into `|0>`\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "qc = QuantumCircuit(1, 1)\n",
                "qc.x(0)\n",
                "qc.measure(0, 0)\n",
                "\n",
                "qc.draw(\"mpl\")\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "result = simulator.run(qc, shots=1024).result()\n",
                "counts = result.get_counts()\n",
                "\n",
                "counts\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Expected result: almost all measurements should return `1`.\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 4. The Hadamard Gate and Superposition\n",
                "\n",
                "The Hadamard gate creates a superposition.\n",
                "\n",
                "Starting from `|0>`, applying H creates a state that has approximately equal probability of being measured as `0` or `1`.\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "qc = QuantumCircuit(1, 1)\n",
                "qc.h(0)\n",
                "qc.measure(0, 0)\n",
                "\n",
                "qc.draw(\"mpl\")\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": None,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "result = simulator.run(qc, shots=1024).result()\n",
                "counts = result.get_counts()\n",
                "\n",
                "counts\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Expected result: approximately 50% `0` and 50% `1`.\n",
                "\n",
                "This does not mean that the computer randomly chooses before measurement. The qubit is in a quantum state whose measurement outcomes are probabilistic.\n"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 5. A Two-Qubit Circuit\n",
